commit f34374f0cdc6ef98e77f18aa335c2ee57ded6bda
Author:     Henry Cikanek <cikanekhenry@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: 2025-11-03
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: 2025-11-04

    fix(chat): Enable task selection in task mode [EVO-2258]
    
    * feat: Add streaming chat functionality
    
    Implements real-time streaming chat using Server-Sent Events (SSE) for responsive user experience.
    
    Core Implementation:
    - streamChatWithAI function with native fetch API and SSE parsing
    - useStreamingChat hook for managing streaming state and lifecycle
    - Event parsing for data, metadata, done, and error events
    - Intelligent throttling (75ms intervals) for smooth UI updates
    
    User Experience:
    - Real-time text streaming directly to UI
    - Optimized render cycle via callbacks
    - Memoized components preventing unnecessary re-renders
    - Rate-limited UI updates (50ms minimum between renders)
    - Enhanced list detection and rendering
    - Improved message formatting with semantic HTML
    
    Configuration:
    - NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_CHAT_STREAMING: Toggle streaming on/off
    - NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_TO_NON_STREAMING: Fallback behavior
    - Backward compatible feature flag system
    
    Files Modified:
    - lib/api/aiApi.ts, lib/api/endpoints.ts
    - lib/hooks/useStreamingChat.ts (new)
    - components/chatbot/* (integration and display)
    - types/chatbot.ts
    - docs/STREAMING_CHAT_IMPLEMENTATION.md (new)
    - README.md
    
    Code Quality:
    - Removed debug logs
    - Fixed ESLint warnings
    - Added TypeScript types
    
    Resolves: EVO-2258
    
    * feat(task-mode): Add task generation endpoint [EVO-2258]
    
    * fix(chat): Enable task selection in task mode [EVO-2258]
    
    - Remove React.memo from ChatMessage and MessageRenderer components
      to allow re-renders when task selection state changes
    - Replace failing crypto.randomUUID() with reliable timestamp-based
      ID generator for client-side task identification
    - Fix individual task selection by ensuring each task gets unique _tempId
    - Apply ID generation across all task handlers (streaming, non-streaming,
      and task mode endpoints)
    
    This resolves visual feedback issues where clicking tasks showed no
    selection state changes, and fixes the bug where selecting one task
    would incorrectly select all tasks due to empty/duplicate IDs.
    
    * fix(chat): Improve task UX and add duplicate prevention [EVO-2258]
    
    - Fixed auto-scroll behavior: scrolls during typing, disables after task messages display
    - Fixed task list messages disappearing from chat when tasks are accepted
    - Fixed loading indicator in task mode
    - Fixed old conversation issues: auto-scroll on load and individual task selection
    - Added aiGeneratedTaskId field to ChatTask interface and task creation payload
    - Added debug logging to trace aiGeneratedTaskId through data flow
    - Backend team fixed chatTasksController to return tasks with UUIDs
    
    Files: useChatActions.ts, ArtiChat.tsx, ChatContext.tsx, chatbot.ts
    
    * refactor(chat): Replace isInteractingWithTasks with disableAutoScrollRef
    
    - Removed isInteractingWithTasks state from ChatContext
    - Removed setIsInteractingWithTasks from useChatActions interface
    - Updated auto-scroll logic to rely solely on disableAutoScrollRef
    - Added disableAutoScrollRef support to artichat page
    - Cleaned up @ts-expect-error comments
    
    Simplifies the auto-scroll control mechanism by using a single ref.
    
    [EVO-2258]
    
    * fix(chat): Show loading indicator in task mode
    
    - Added setCurrentTypingMessage(null) at start of handleTaskGenerationTaskMode
    - Added setCurrentTypingMessage(null) at start of handleTaskGenerationNonStreaming
    - Ensures loading indicator displays while waiting for task generation response
    
    Previously, if a previous message had set currentTypingMessage, it would
    prevent the loading indicator from showing due to the condition
    isTyping && !currentTypingMessage evaluating to false.
    
    [EVO-2258]

